  "worked_solution": "Trigonometric functions are continuous at all points in their respective domains.\n\nThe function $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x$ is continuous over the entire interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ but the function $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x$ is not defined at $x=-\\pi ,0,\\pi .$ \n\nTherefore, the domain of $g(x)$ consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\pi ,0)$ and $(0,\\pi ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\pi ,0)\\cup (0,\\pi )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
